    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d474">

                <pb facs="1031" n="999" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v15/pg999"/>

                <head>474. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Thailand<anchor n="1" xml:id="d474-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1958-05-07T17:32:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 7,
                                1958—5:32 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2779. Call of Sarit on President May 7, in
                    which Robertson, Thai Ambassador and
                    Colonel Chalermchai participated, carried out in utmost cordiality.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d474-f2"/>
                    Sarit delivered to President greetings
                    from Thai Government and his thanks for hospitality and excellent medical
                    treatment received Walter Reed. He discussed with President
                    broad outlines Thai situation and problems including in most general fashion
                    need for increased aid. President indicated that Mr. Robertson and other appropriate US officials would have
                    subsequent discussions with him these matters.</p>
                <p>Extensive photographic coverage given meeting, which lasted about twenty minutes.
                    Department release re Sarit visit<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d474-f3"/> carried on <pb facs="1032" n="1000" xml:id="pg1000"
                    /> VOA morning broadcast. According UP Sarit told press President “most sympathetic” with Thailand’s
                    problems.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Herter</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d474-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d474-f1-content">
